            <ArticleTitle>Right coronary ostium agenesis with absence of the right coronary artery: a rare case of non-ST elevation coronary syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>345-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case with right coronary ostium agenesis with anomalous origin of the right coronary artery from the left circumflex artery, which caused a non-ST elevation coronary syndrome. A review of the literature indicates this to be an extremely rare case.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
